  "body": "A model-group request can stop early on NVIDIA NIM's HTTP 400 `Validation: Unsupported parameter(s): `reasoning`, `enable_thinking`` (backtick-quoted field names), even though later members remain available.\n\nObserved on Docker 0.1.1472: two members timed out, then NVIDIA rejected the request parameters; the client received 400 and stopped its task. NVIDIA was tried once, not three times. Current upstream's request-shape matcher also misses this message.\n\nExpected: after existing safe compatibility handling has been exhausted, treat an explicit unsupported-field rejection as request-shape incompatibility: try the next member without resting the key/account/model. Keep an unrepairable request's fields intact for the next member. Do not classify every 400/422 or every invalid value this way; do not feed this into generic failure backoff.\n\nRegression coverage should exercise the actual group handler, prove the next member succeeds, bound calls to the rejecting member, and assert that no cooldown is added. This is separate from teaching optional-field compatibility to repair redundant ZCode parameters.",
  "closed_by": null,
