   "updated_at": "2026-10-25T17:11:08Z",
   "body": "Fork fix: [continue groups after explicit parameter-list refusals](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/commit/0d3dca3dabaacf3b9a1452e1762e261f86b82f2b).\n\nThis builds on the parameter-list reader in [#3635's compatibility commit](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/commit/ad3badd3abe13b4adff86f3fa48fd70c291d416f). It uses structured error parsing in both failure detection and request-shape classification, including provider-prefixed messages and JSON-escaped delimiters. After safe compatibility handling, an unresolved explicit list goes to the next group member through the existing shape branch, without generic cooldown/backoff.\n\n`TestGroupFailsOverUnsupportedParameterList` exercises the real group handler for both 400 and 422: two successive requests each try the rejecting member once, then succeed on the next; the rejected attempt has `failShape` and no rest. Its richer reasoning settings are deliberately ineligible for stripping. Removing the fix makes the test fail because the next member is never called. Invalid-value input echoes are negative cases; escaped delimiters have a separate regression.\n\n[Branch](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/nvidia-parameters-routing) · [Validation](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/blob/055637f4dccc2b9a843a52a5456aab3f41fa64f5/VALIDATION.md).\n\nTargeted regressions and all six vet/build checks pass. Full-suite failures and baseline comparisons are recorded explicitly; the complete suite is not claimed green. No production deployment or cooldown-policy expansion was performed.",
   "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
