     "body": "ZCode's default Chat mapping can send `thinking`, `enable_thinking`, `reasoning_effort`, and `reasoning` together. NVIDIA NIM returns HTTP 400: `Validation: Unsupported parameter(s): `reasoning`, `enable_thinking`` (field names are backtick-quoted).\n\nMagpie already retries explicitly unsupported optional fields, but its parser misses this list syntax and `reasoning` is not handled as a redundant alias. Observed with Step-5-preview and GLM-5.3-flash on Docker 0.1.1472; the relevant gap remains in current upstream source.\n\nExpected: recognize the explicitly named top-level fields and reuse existing compatibility retry. Drop `reasoning` only when it is exactly an effort-only object equivalent to a retained nonempty `reasoning_effort`; preserve sole, conflicting, or richer reasoning settings. The same condition must hold when applying a remembered compatibility decision on later requests. Do not broadly strip reasoning controls, reinterpret invalid values as unsupported fields, or change cooldown policy.\n\nA separate issue covers switching group members when safe compatibility repair is unavailable or fails. Sanitized fixture: request includes `\"reasoning_effort\":\"high\", \"reasoning\":{\"effort\":\"high\"}, \"enable_thinking\":true, \"thinking\":{\"type\":\"enabled\"}`; error message as above. Private conversation exports are omitted.",
